cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation, please cite the software release."
type: software
title: "Riemann Hypothesis Lean Formalisation"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: 2026-08-25
authors:
  - name: "ArtiFish26"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/artifish26/riemann-hypothesis-lean"
url: "https://github.com/artifish26/riemann-hypothesis-lean"
abstract: >-
  A Lean and Mathlib formalisation of multiplicity-aware zero counting,
  polynomial-Gaussian zero-side summability, a selected Guinand-Weil formula,
  Li/Bombieri-Lagarias equivalences, fixed-support Burnol positivity, a formal
  Hardy theorem proving infinitely many nontrivial critical-line zeros, and
  an experimental Suzuki S4 compact-window solution family. The accompanying
  RIG1 annular theorem is paper-level rather than Lean-checked. Global Weil/Li
  positivity and the Riemann Hypothesis remain open.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - Riemann zeta function
  - Guinand-Weil explicit formula
  - Li criterion
  - Suzuki operator
  - compact-window coercivity
  - Hardy theorem
  - critical-line zeros
  - formalised mathematics
